      "@id": "kt:ford-model-t",
      "@type": "kto:Case",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Ford Model T",
      "skos:definition": "The low-priced automobile Ford Motor Company built from 1908 to 1927, whose moving assembly line, relentless price cuts and five-dollar day made it the classic case of mass production, scale economies and, ultimately, the risks of a single-product strategy against GM's annual model change.",
